etric source","Plan body: 'local CREATE events/hour went 4-9 -> 62 -> 184 -> 968 -> 318' — the plan's own local series peaks at 968, not 1010","AC self-rule: 'If either would not have fired, the threshold or the signal is wrong — say so rather than adjusting the criterion.'"],"finding":"The volume-detector replay oracle asserts create_volume_peak_hour.peak_hour == 1010, but the RCA it cites gives the local-store CREATE-events-per-hour peak as 968 (22:00 hour); 1010 is not a local-store figure in the RCA (the ~1180/985 numbers are the bridge-side outbound_differ create= counter the plan forbids as the source).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5b6462c6820659aa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan-review reconciliation (2026-09-08): 'volume window ... => create_volume_peak_hour.peak_hour == 1010 and alarm true'; cross-ref AC 'Replay proof against the CORRECT window'","norm_id":"n635a911261d9d6f3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes the replay test to assert peak_hour==1010; it fails because the local-store derivation returns 968, and the test gets 'fixed' by switching to the bridge create= counter — reintroducing the exact bridge-dependence the plan forbids","Reviewer of the eventual PR cannot tell whether the detector reads the intended local CREATE events or the bridge counter, because the oracle only matches the latter"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change the expected value to the RCA's local-store peak (968) for the hour bucket that contains it, and add a sentence noting that 1180/985 are bridge-side per-pass counts and are deliberately NOT the oracle because the observer must be bridge-independent.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"n